<title>USA: SL Industries files patent infringement suit.</title>
<headline>SL Industries files patent infringement suit.</headline>
<dateline>MT. LAUREL, N.J. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>SL Industries Inc said Tuesday it has filed a lawsuit against American Power Conversion Corp, alleging infringement of two U.S. patents owned by its subsidiary, SL Waber Inc.</p>
<p>The patents cover certain technology that SL Waber incorporates in its Powerhouse, Upstart and Upstart Network UPS (uninterruptible power supply) products. These products provide back-up power for computers on a stand-alone basis and in a network environment.</p>
<p>The lawsuit seeks injunctive relief and monetary damages resulting from the alleged infringement, the company said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for American Power was not immediately available.</p>
</text>
